1
00:00:18,839 --> 00:00:19,719
In the early 1980s,

2
00:00:20,199 --> 00:00:22,280
the market economy was just emerging in Songliao.

3
00:00:22,719 --> 00:00:24,579
Supply and demand still relied on rationing.

4
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,899
Money alone wasn't enough to buy things.

5
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,239
You needed coupons, too.

6
00:00:28,899 --> 00:00:30,100
Since I had no coal coupons,

7
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,439
I asked around and found a private coal yard.

8
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,640
Back then, that was called Profiteering.

9
00:00:35,979 --> 00:00:37,340
Folks also called it...

10
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:38,520
the black market.

11
00:00:40,119 --> 00:00:41,100
Is this where I buy coal?

12
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:43,340
Where's your money?

13
00:00:55,079 --> 00:00:55,600
Hurry up!

14
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:08,260
What, mine's too expensive?

15
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:09,939
Then fine, don't buy it.

16
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:10,959
Right now,

17
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:13,000
go line up at the state coal station.

18
00:01:13,519 --> 00:01:14,840
For someone like you without coal coupons,

19
00:01:15,299 --> 00:01:16,840
wait in line till spring and see

20
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:17,819
if they'll even sell to you.

21
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:18,900
Buddy,

22
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,599
you're playing dumb here, aren't you?

23
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:22,680
Those bastards who used to sell in North City,

24
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,359
how much were they charging?

25
00:01:23,359 --> 00:01:24,739
Over two mao a jin, right?

26
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:27,040
Now coal's down to one and a half mao.

27
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,700
Isn't that fair enough?

28
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:30,840
Let me tell you, old-timer,

29
00:01:30,859 --> 00:01:32,140
while coal prices are good,

30
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,140
hurry up and stock up on more.

31
00:01:33,459 --> 00:01:35,159
Once my supply runs short later on,

32
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,280
who knows how high the price will go.

33
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,819
Count your blessings you can even buy it.

34
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,280
What are you doing?

35
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:56,239
How can the weight be right if you do that?

36
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:00,840
It's right on.

37
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:01,819
It's right on.

38
00:02:02,599 --> 00:02:03,400
Just leave it.

39
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:04,879
We're lucky to even have coal.

40
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:10,199
Next in line!

41
00:02:14,979 --> 00:02:16,460
How much you want, pal?

42
00:02:18,099 --> 00:02:18,939
Give me 500 jin.

43
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:20,620
We've got rules around here.

44
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,300
First-timers...

45
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:24,020
must buy at least one ton.

46
00:02:26,439 --> 00:02:27,340
What about that old man just now?

47
00:02:27,419 --> 00:02:28,460
That was then, this is now.

48
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,979
I was in a good mood back then.

49
00:02:31,699 --> 00:02:32,419
Now, as you can see...

50
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,259
I'm not too happy.

51
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,219
So the price went up.

52
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:38,280
It's two mao a jin now.

53
00:02:38,699 --> 00:02:39,680
If you're not buying...

54
00:02:39,759 --> 00:02:40,860
step aside.

55
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:43,659
Jacking up the price on the spot, huh?

56
00:02:44,379 --> 00:02:44,919
So what?

57
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,139
My coal...

58
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,400
my turf...

59
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,020
I do whatever the hell I want.

60
00:02:55,479 --> 00:02:56,360
Price gouging...

61
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:00,280
and using a rigged scale.

62
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:02,560
Think you're real tough, huh?

63
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:04,520
What?

64
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,939
I've been watching you for a while.

65
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:08,219
What?

66
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,259
You come here to bust up my spot?

67
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,060
Do you even know whose turf this is?

68
00:03:13,419 --> 00:03:14,520
Causing trouble on my turf...

69
00:03:14,639 --> 00:03:16,699
Pal, what the hell are you thinking?

70
00:03:17,979 --> 00:03:19,000
Relying on your numbers, huh?

71
00:03:19,319 --> 00:03:20,379
Damn right we've got the numbers.

72
00:03:59,979 --> 00:04:00,539
Bro,

73
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:01,939
you're back.

74
00:04:02,379 --> 00:04:03,759
This bastard is trashing our place!

75
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,919
Got a big deal going on today, huh?

76
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:14,919
So you're the one in charge?

77
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,720
Wearing pitch-black glasses like that...

78
00:04:18,779 --> 00:04:19,779
can you even see where you're going?

79
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:21,459
Cut the crap, or I'll beat your ass!

80
00:04:21,459 --> 00:04:21,899
Daguang.

81
00:04:39,899 --> 00:04:40,680
Long time no see.

82
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:42,480
You're quite the fighter, huh?

83
00:04:43,939 --> 00:04:44,759
Liu Haizhu.

84
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:51,279
Hardly.

85
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:58,639
What about that girl?

86
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,639
How is she doing?

87
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,060
She's his sister.

88
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,019
Chen Baige.

89
00:05:07,519 --> 00:05:09,279
She's doing great these days.

90
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:10,500
Full of life.

91
00:05:10,579 --> 00:05:11,199
Only thing is,

92
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:12,620
her temper's gotten worse.

93
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:13,199
Yeah.

94
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:16,740
Ain't that something.

95
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,759
How many years has it been already?

96
00:05:20,139 --> 00:05:21,259
What a coincidence.

97
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:23,120
Never thought we'd run into each other here today.

98
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:26,019
Yeah.

99
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:29,839
"Sing while drinking, for life is short."

100
00:05:32,079 --> 00:05:34,000
Why bust out classical poetry all of a sudden?

101
00:05:37,199 --> 00:05:39,860
I remember you looking so refined back then,

102
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,040
like a student.

103
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,579
How did you...

104
00:05:44,339 --> 00:05:46,860
How'd you end up a Profiteering peddler?

105
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:47,939
What are you talking about?

106
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,399
The name "Tyrant of the East"—

107
00:05:50,519 --> 00:05:52,100
you never heard of it in Songliao?

108
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:53,920
Tyrant of the East?

109
00:05:55,459 --> 00:05:55,839
That's right.

110
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:57,480
Peddler?

111
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,720
Just a small-time peddler.

112
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:00,620
Just scraping by, you know?

113
00:06:02,699 --> 00:06:04,079
No need to be so humble.

114
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:06,120
Looks like you run quite an operation.

115
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:10,160
So today,

116
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:13,360
how did you guys end up fighting?

117
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:29,639
Mengmeng.

118
00:06:30,959 --> 00:06:31,620
Mengmeng!

119
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,379
What are you still doing here?

120
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:36,019
I'm waiting... waiting for someone.

121
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,420
Liu Haizhu?

122
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:42,800
Come on, let's go.

123
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:43,800
He'll find you when he gets here.

124
00:06:44,079 --> 00:06:44,459
Let's go.

125
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,259
B-But...

126
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:46,680
I already saved our seats.

127
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,019
Is that rigged scale thing real?

128
00:06:53,639 --> 00:06:54,480
Who's in charge of the scales?

129
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,160
Bro...

130
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:01,860
Me.

131
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:17,579
Here's a ring for you.

132
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,060
Put it on.

133
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:20,939
What are you doing, bro?

134
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,620
Aren't we friends? We've talked it out.

135
00:07:22,639 --> 00:07:23,160
There's no need for this.

136
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:23,819
Seriously, bro.

137
00:07:24,879 --> 00:07:27,259
Look, I still make some cash on the side.

138
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,459
There's really no need.

139
00:07:56,699 --> 00:07:57,579
A man of honor seeks wealth,

140
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,339
but earns it the right way.

141
00:08:00,899 --> 00:08:01,519
Yang Wu,

142
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:03,120
as long as you play by the rules,

143
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:04,839
we're still brothers.

144
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,379
Excuse me, Comrade.

145
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:14,800
This seat is taken.

146
00:08:14,959 --> 00:08:16,040
Isn't this a public place?

147
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,060
Does it have your name on it?

148
00:08:18,259 --> 00:08:19,680
Who does he think he is? Seriously.

149
00:08:19,899 --> 00:08:21,540
I'm the one who brought this stool over.

150
00:08:22,379 --> 00:08:23,019
Forget it, let it go.

151
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:23,860
Unbelievable!

152
00:08:23,899 --> 00:08:24,819
Right? What a jerk.

153
00:08:24,939 --> 00:08:25,740
Stealing someone's seat like that.

154
00:08:25,819 --> 00:08:27,199
Why isn't Zhuzi here yet?

155
00:08:28,319 --> 00:08:28,839
All right, that's enough.

156
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,439
No need to see me out.

157
00:08:29,579 --> 00:08:30,000
Head on back.

158
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:30,600
Zhuzi,

159
00:08:31,879 --> 00:08:34,179
aren't you gonna grab a bite with a peddler like me

160
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,000
and catch up?

161
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:37,080
I've really got things to do today.

162
00:08:37,259 --> 00:08:38,399
If I don't leave now, I'll be late.

163
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:41,620
Tyrant of the East...

164
00:09:06,159 --> 00:09:07,899
You really got the nerve to steal my business?

165
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,039
He...

166
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,860
...is in your line of work, too.

167
00:09:14,519 --> 00:09:14,960
Zhuzi,

168
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:16,500
let me put your skills to work.

169
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:20,700
We'll share the wealth,

170
00:09:20,779 --> 00:09:21,860
and take the heat together.

171
00:09:23,899 --> 00:09:25,000
You're my brother!

172
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:26,720
Take him down!

173
00:10:01,899 --> 00:10:03,399
Hello, everyone.

174
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,899
I'm a teacher from Songliao No. 1 Middle School.

175
00:10:06,139 --> 00:10:07,240
My name is Feng Menglong.

176
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:08,279
Bravo!

177
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,720
Bravo! Bravo!

178
00:10:13,179 --> 00:10:13,799
Today,

179
00:10:14,059 --> 00:10:15,500
I'd like to recite

180
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:16,720
a poem I wrote myself.

181
00:10:17,019 --> 00:10:18,059
The title of the poem is

182
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,740
"That Day, I Kept Crying."

183
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:28,980
Golden millet

184
00:10:29,779 --> 00:10:31,220
spilled into my eyes.

185
00:10:32,559 --> 00:10:33,179
And so,

186
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,320
I began to cry.

187
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:38,299
Golden tears

188
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:40,960
dripped onto Mother's chapped hands.

189
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,379
Gray-black newspaper

190
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:45,220
caught my eye.

191
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:46,299
And so,

192
00:10:46,919 --> 00:10:48,039
I continued to cry.

193
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:50,779
Gray-black tears

194
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:53,200
dripped onto this

195
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,500
vast, boundless land.

196
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,639
Pure white snowflakes

197
00:10:58,299 --> 00:10:59,740
drifted across my vision.

198
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:01,879
And so,

199
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,600
I was still crying.

200
00:11:05,019 --> 00:11:06,159
Rough hands

201
00:11:06,679 --> 00:11:08,419
caressed my face.

202
00:11:09,019 --> 00:11:11,220
The dried riverbeds of those fingerprints

203
00:11:11,820 --> 00:11:13,580
scratched my skin.

204
00:11:14,419 --> 00:11:16,299
Wind slipped through my fingers.

205
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,059
I reached out,

206
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,080
but caught nothing.

207
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:21,500
And so,

208
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,320
I kept crying.

209
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:26,360
I love the people of this land.

210
00:11:26,919 --> 00:11:28,879
I love their five millennia of kindness,

211
00:11:30,139 --> 00:11:31,580
their eternal longing,

212
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,580
and their hope.

213
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:36,759
That day,

214
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:39,820
I kept crying,

215
00:11:41,519 --> 00:11:42,580
kept on crying.

216
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:45,759
Bravo! Bravo!

217
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:47,799
Teacher Feng, that was wonderful!

218
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:53,820
Comrade,

219
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:55,100
what are you laughing at?

220
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,919
You call that a poem?

221
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:58,980
If mine isn't a poem,

222
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:00,700
then tell me,

223
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:02,460
what is?

224
00:12:20,299 --> 00:12:24,220
The Third Plenum is so great,

225
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:29,259
The working masses' spirits elevate!

226
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:31,700
What kind of poem is that?

227
00:12:31,899 --> 00:12:34,700
Five Stresses, Four Beauties, and Three Loves,

228
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,720
Every household will raise

229
00:12:40,379 --> 00:12:41,960
a giant panda!

230
00:12:44,299 --> 00:12:45,559
Get off! Get off the stage!

231
00:12:46,059 --> 00:12:47,740
You look like a panda yourself!

232
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,019
Get off the stage already!

233
00:12:49,639 --> 00:12:51,379
You're just a petty clown!

234
00:12:51,779 --> 00:12:52,799
Completely ridiculous!

235
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:54,580
The last line should be:

236
00:12:54,679 --> 00:12:56,620
"Clumsy mimics only draw ridicule!"

237
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:58,539
That's right! Exactly!

238
00:12:58,919 --> 00:13:00,659
Get down, hurry!

239
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,240
What the hell do you know, broad?

240
00:13:04,299 --> 00:13:05,080
Shut your mouth! Comrade—

241
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:05,539
Shut up!

242
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:06,779
Foul-mouthed jerk! Let go!

243
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:07,639
Please leave immediately!

244
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:08,080
Get out!

245
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:08,899
You... Get the hell out!

246
00:13:08,899 --> 00:13:10,080
What is wrong with you?

247
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:10,820
You cursed at her!

248
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,860
He's shoving people! Don't make me hit you!

249
00:13:13,639 --> 00:13:14,419
He's pulling my hair!

250
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,620
Feng Menglong, I'll remember this!

251
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:19,820
Serves you right!

252
00:13:19,879 --> 00:13:20,379
Down he goes!

253
00:13:21,679 --> 00:13:22,639
I'm gonna get my boys right now!

254
00:13:22,679 --> 00:13:23,340
You wait right here for me!

255
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:24,019
Got that?

256
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,879
Just get the hell out!

257
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,700
Beat it, hurry!

258
00:13:35,059 --> 00:13:35,940
Nice going.

259
00:13:42,659 --> 00:13:43,899
Are you trying to get me killed?

260
00:13:45,379 --> 00:13:46,820
I'm sorry, I'm really sorry!

261
00:13:47,259 --> 00:13:48,100
What kind of show was that?

262
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,139
What kind of people are they?

263
00:13:50,039 --> 00:13:51,360
Just everyday life for street peddlers.

264
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:52,580
This illicit coal business...

265
00:13:52,779 --> 00:13:54,000
I snatched it right out of his hands.

266
00:13:54,399 --> 00:13:55,259
The price he was charging before

267
00:13:55,299 --> 00:13:56,139
was several times higher than mine.

268
00:13:56,799 --> 00:13:58,019
I'm a vendor with a conscience.

269
00:14:00,899 --> 00:14:01,419
Tyrant of the East...

270
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:04,279
Do you guys really think I'm scared of you?

271
00:14:04,399 --> 00:14:04,899
Well?

272
00:14:15,039 --> 00:14:15,720
If you're a real man,

273
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,759
let's go one-on-one! Come on!

274
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:17,600
Come on, get over here! Come on!

275
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:18,360
Come on!

276
00:14:19,179 --> 00:14:20,139
Take one more step, I dare you.

277
00:14:23,759 --> 00:14:24,740
Take one more step and see what happens!

278
00:14:26,899 --> 00:14:27,580
Brother Ziwen!

279
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:29,039
Bro, I'm back.

280
00:14:34,799 --> 00:14:35,379
Don't move!
